#: ui/pages.slint:2409
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid "Unlock protection"
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2410
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid ""
"How much work each guess at your master password costs, for you once per "
"unlock and for anyone with a copy of the vault file every time they guess."
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2411
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid ""
"Your master password is stretched before it opens the vault. Argon2id is the "
"method recommended today (RFC 9106, OWASP): it needs a lot of memory for "
"every guess, which is what makes graphics cards and special chips slow at "
"guessing. scrypt also needs memory but is older. PBKDF2-SHA-256 needs almost "
"none, so it is the weakest of the three; it is here for people who must "
"follow a rule that names it. Higher levels cost more per guess. Changing the "
"method or level rewrites only the password lock of the vault, never your "
"items."
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2417
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid ""
"Weaker than Argon2id: scrypt also needs memory for every guess, but it is "
"older and special hardware does better against it. Keep Argon2id unless you "
"have a reason."
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2418
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid ""
"Much weaker than Argon2id: PBKDF2 needs almost no memory, so graphics cards "
"guess thousands of times faster against it. Choose it only if you must, and "
"then a long master password matters even more."
msgstr ""

