#: ui/pages.slint:2824
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid "Offer to save logins typed into pages"
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2831
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid ""
"After you sign in on a page, the extension offers to save the login here, or "
"to update its password when it changed. Logins saved while the vault is "
"locked wait, sealed, and join it at the next unlock. Off, nothing is offered "
"or saved from the browser."
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2839
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid "Make and use passkeys from this vault"
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2846
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid ""
"When a site makes a passkey, it is saved in the login for that site, in this "
"vault, and syncs with it; when a site asks for one, this vault answers. You "
"see a login's passkeys on its page. Off, the browser handles passkeys as "
"before."
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2854
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid "Fill with Windows Hello while the vault is locked"
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2861
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid ""
"The app keeps the passwords of your logins for the extension in a file only "
"Windows Hello opens, so a locked vault can still fill: each password asks "
"for your face, fingerprint or Windows PIN. The item lock's PIN does not work "
"here, because a copied file could be tried against every PIN away from this "
"app. It needs Windows Hello on in Item lock and the app running (closed to "
"the notification area is fine). Usernames and websites stay readable to your "
"Windows account so the extension can list them."
msgstr ""

